@startuml
title Facade | How the console uses the same application boundary
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam ArrowColor #40546E
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F5F7FB
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #40546E
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 250
hide footbox

participant ConsoleClient as Console
participant LanguageLearningFacade as Facade
participant StudySession as Cards
participant ReviewClient as Reviews
participant LessonBuilderClient as Builder
participant LessonSession as Practice
participant ProgressFacade as Progress
participant "ProgressRepository\n(FileProgressRepository)" as Storage
participant "ProgressSubject\n(ProgressPublisher)" as Events

note over Console, Facade
  ConsoleClient depends on LearningApplication.
  LanguageLearningFacade implements that contract.
end note

group Start a lesson: read and confirm one card
  Console -> Facade : startLesson(topic, count)
  note right of Facade : Select topic words, unseen first.
  Facade -> Cards : new StudySession(topic, words)
  Facade --> Console : StudySession
  note left of Console : Show word, translation and example.
  Console -> Facade : learnCurrentWord() [Enter]
  Facade -> Progress : recordStudy(current word, last card?)
  Progress -> Storage : save(next snapshot)
  Storage --> Progress : saved
  Progress --> Facade : return
  Facade -> Cards : advance()
  Facade -> Progress : notifyObservers()
  Progress -> Events : publish(saved snapshot)
  note over Progress, Storage
    A new card becomes studied and due today.
    No answer attempt or XP is added.
    Final-card completion is saved in the same snapshot.
  end note
end

group Practice words: create a session and submit one answer
  Console -> Facade : startReview(strategy, count, mode)
  Facade -> Reviews : selectForPractice(strategy, vocabulary, progress, count, today)
  Reviews --> Facade : exact requested word list
  Facade -> Builder : create(title, "Review", words, vocabulary, mode)
  Builder --> Facade : Lesson
  Facade -> Practice : new LessonSession(lesson)
  Facade --> Console : LessonSession
  Console -> Facade : submitAnswer(answer)
  Facade -> Progress : recordAnswer(current exercise, answer)
  Progress -> Storage : save(next snapshot)
  Storage --> Progress : saved
  Progress --> Facade : AnswerResult
  Facade -> Practice : record(correct, xp)
  Facade -> Progress : notifyObservers()
  Progress -> Events : publish(saved snapshot)
  Facade --> Console : AnswerResult
end

note over Facade, Storage
  These are successful-save paths. If saving throws IOException,
  the facade does not advance the card or record the answer in the session,
  and it does not publish the unsaved progress. The console can retry.
  Practice advancement/completion happens separately through nextExercise().
end note
@enduml
